== Part F: Rong-Halpern M-PCE in G2 (exact, BU from Nash equilibria of the residual game) ==
BU = (1/7, -1/7, 13/7)
min(u1 - 1/7, u2 + 1/7) <= 0 with equality iff u1 = 1/7 (cross); so max of min_i(u_i - BU_i) is 0, reached
on the cross where u3 >= 13/7: {(3/7,q): q <= 2/7} U {(p,2/7): p <= 3/7}
  (3/7,0): u3 = 15/7, min gain = 0
  (3/7,2/7): u3 = 13/7, min gain = 0
  (0,2/7): u3 = 19/7, min gain = 0
=> the M-PCE (3/7,2/7) is Pareto-dominated by the M-PCE (3/7,0): not every M-PCE is Pareto-optimal.
three players: BU = (2,2,1) (player 1 commits to a, player 3's dominant Y, player 2 answers a; symmetric for player 2; player 3's Y gives 1); v^m = (0,0,1) (Y guarantees 1 to player 3; the others can be held to 0)
  (a, a, 2/3 X + 1/3 Y): u = (2, 5/3, 2/3), min_i (u_i - BU_i) = -1/3
  grid 101^3: max of min_i (u_i - BU_i) = -0.3350 at (p,q,r) = (1.00, 1.00, 0.67); player 3 gets 0.6650 there
  every grid maximizer gives player 3 less than v_3^m = 1: True
coordination (a,a) -> (2,2), (b,b) -> (1,1), mismatch (0,0); dummy gets 0, 10 at (b,b), 0: BU = (2,2,10); B = {(a,a)} with min_i (u_i - BU_i) = -10, while (b,b) has -1: B is not inside M-PCE

